cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "jsonW: a data format for the AI era"
message: "If you use jsonW in research or in a product, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: Wortic
    website: "https://wortic.com.br"
version: 1.4.2
date-released: 2026-11-14
url: "https://jsonw.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/developer-wortic/jsonw"
license-url: "https://github.com/developer-wortic/jsonw/blob/main/LICENCA.md"
abstract: >-
  jsonW (json Wondrous) is a data format and zero-dependency C library with three lossless forms of the same data:
  text (every valid JSON is valid jsonW-text), binary row and columnar file (.jsw). It has business types (money with
  currency, exact decimals, units of measure, exact codes), typed embeddings and tensors, and 19 built-in features
  including term and semantic search, top-k ranking, key index, column/row/cell permissions, tamper-evident custody and
  partial remote reads over HTTP Range.
keywords:
  - data format
  - JSON alternative
  - Parquet alternative
  - columnar storage
  - vector search
  - embeddings
  - RAG
  - serialization
  - multi-tenant
  - data custody
